{
  "name": "onboarding",
  "description": "Developer onboarding and first-time setup for the Barrits monorepo. Use for new contributors, environment setup, project structure explanation, and development workflow introduction.",
  "prompts": [
    {
      "name": "setup-dev",
      "description": "Full development environment setup checklist for new contributors.",
      "prompt": "Guide the user through: 1) git clone the repo, 2) npm install from root (workspaces auto-install), 3) cd packages/sdk/ts_js && npm run build, 4) npm test to verify 935+ tests passing (0 expected failures). Check: Node >=18 (v22+ recommended), Deno >=2.x, Bun >=1.3 (optional), Git, VS Code with ESLint extension. For PowerShell users: use 'node F:\\path\\to\\node_modules\\tsx\\dist\\cli.mjs' instead of npx for manual runs."
    },
    {
      "name": "project-structure",
      "description": "Explain the monorepo layout, key directories, and where to find important files.",
      "prompt": "Root: AGENTS.md (agent operational rules), REPOSITORY_CONTEXT.md (canonical context), CHANGELOG.md, docs/ (bilingual documentation). packages/sdk/ts_js/ is the main SDK (@zuccadev-labs/barrits v0.1.9). src/barrits/ has the core engine: api/ (flat, hybrid, factory, domains), sdk/ (discovery, inspect, imports, manifest, query, consume, guards, cli-parser, completions), traits/ (descriptor composition), plugins/ (vite, esbuild, rollup, webpack), internal/ (config normalization), ioc/ (IoC container). adapters/ has node/ and deno/ CLI implementations. tests/ mirrors source layout. examples/ has 11 integration examples. .opencode/skills/ has 9 agent skills. docs/agents/skills/ has 11 narrative SKILL.md files."
    },
    {
      "name": "first-contribution",
      "description": "Step-by-step guide for making a first code contribution to Barrits.",
      "prompt": "1) Read AGENTS.md and REPOSITORY_CONTEXT.md. 2) git checkout -b feat/<description> from dev. 3) Make changes following architecture patterns (SRP: domain logic in barrits/, utilities in barrits_lib/). 4) npm run typecheck (0 errors), npm run lint (0 errors/warnings), npm test (all passing). 5) Update CHANGELOG.md under [Unreleased]. 6) git add -A && git commit -m 'feat(scope): description'. 7) gh pr create --base dev. For detailed workflow, reference docs/agents/skills/barrits-contribution-workflow/."
    }
  ]
}
